<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ indexed bonds yield 5.19 percent at tender.</title>
<headline>NZ indexed bonds yield 5.19 percent at tender.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The allocation yield on New Zealand government inflation-indexed February 2016 bonds at Thursday's tender was 5.19 percent, the Reserve Bank said.</p>
<p>The tender was for NZ$50 million of the bonds, which have a 4.50 percent coupon.</p>
<p>Bids totalled NZ$172 million.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
